<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<lint>
    <!--
      Upstream-release-cadence advisories, not correctness or security checks.
      Each fires purely because a newer version exists upstream, so each turns an
      event entirely outside this repository into a red build on unrelated
      changes. Real vulnerability detection is gated elsewhere and stays fatal:
      dependency-review-action (fail-on-severity: high), cargo-deny check
      advisories, rustsec/audit-check, CodeQL, and Dependabot security alerts.
    -->
    <issue id="GradleDependency" severity="ignore" />
    <issue id="NewerVersionAvailable" severity="ignore" />
    <!--
      Same class as the two above, and demoted for the same reason. Recorded
      explicitly because the reasoning is easy to mistake for weakening a gate:

        $ lint --show AndroidGradlePluginVersion
        Summary: Obsolete Android Gradle Plugin Version
        Priority: 4 / 10
        Severity: Warning
        "Using older versions is fine, and there are cases where you
         deliberately want to stick with an older version. However, you may
         simply not be aware that a more recent version is available, and that
         is what this lint check helps find."

      Lint's own default severity is Warning and its own description states that
      staying on an older version is fine - it is an awareness aid, not a
      requirement. It only became build-breaking here because `warningsAsErrors
      = true` promotes it to an error, which also means demoting it to "warning"
      would be a no-op. "informational" is the weakest demotion that actually
      takes effect, and unlike "ignore" it keeps the advisory visible in every
      lint report, so Gradle currency stays tracked without failing CI every
      time Gradle ships a patch release.

      The wrapper's integrity is independently pinned in
      apps/android/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties by
      distributionSha256Sum plus validateDistributionUrl=true, so demoting this
      advisory does not loosen any check on what actually gets executed.
    -->
    <issue id="AndroidGradlePluginVersion" severity="informational" />
</lint>
